Local rollup of the two upstream follow-up patches
(uaudio-upstream-0001-shared-clock-write-discipline.c.patch and
uaudio-upstream-0002-prefer-explicit-feedback.c.patch), rebased onto this
host's tree, i.e. releng/15.1 + uaudio-clock-before-alt.c.patch +
uaudio-shared-clock-fix.c.patch.

Difference from the upstream pair: because clock-before-alt tracks the
last programmed rate in sc->sc_clock_rate and settles for
hw.usb.uaudio.clock_settle_ms on a change, the GET_CUR read-back replaces
that heuristic instead of standing beside it -- the settling delay is now
applied only when a clock was really written, and the rate is verified
after settling and before the streaming alternate setting arms it.
A write is only ever skipped on the strength of a successful read-back;
on a device that cannot report its rate the SET_CUR goes out exactly as
before, and sc_clock_rate then decides only whether the change is worth
settling for.

Apply with:  cd /usr/src && patch -p1 < uaudio-clock-transaction.c.patch
